      "source_id": "incremental_exponent_state",
      "origin": "discover",
      "kind": "call",
      "change_ids": [
        "g0003"
      ],
      "requirement": "Exercise the parser's saved exponent state restoration by continuing a number through another parse_ex call on the same tokener.",
      "target_route": "For example, call parse_ex on [0e, then call it on -1] using the same tokener; the second call enters the saved-buffer branch and accepts the exponent minus.",
      "failure_condition": "The old entry creates a fresh tokener, makes exactly one parse_ex call, then frees it. No supplied input can make that call resume a number from an earlier call.",
      "alternative_paths": "Other numbers in the same input enter number state after resetting the print buffer; trailing bytes, defaults, and delimiters do not create a second parse_ex call. The complete entry has no helper or reuse route.",
      "discovery_necessary": true,
      "discovery_established": true
    }
  ],
